  "feature": "Private supporting transport documents linked to departure, LR/GR and POD",
  "status": "Implemented and locally verified",
  "behavior": [
    "Both confirmed booking parties may record private goods invoices, bills of supply, delivery challans, e-way bills and pickup/delivery weighbridge slips before the first POD and while no dispute is open.",
    "Each category has a current immutable version, retained original files, reasoned replacements, bounded paged history, current-version conflicts and request-key deduplication.",
    "Original PDFs/JPGs/PNGs are private, at most 5 MB per upload. File hashes are checked before departure and download; stored paths and hashes are omitted from public API DTOs.",
    "Weighbridge net cargo is derived on the server from gross minus positive tare. Client net weight, plate and capacity fields cannot override canonical values.",
    "Pickup net payload or gross weight above the reviewed vehicle limits blocks departure. A lower slip cannot reduce the declared/agreed load weight.",
    "A higher recorded pickup weight must be reflected in an amended LR/GR before departure. Its weight is server-derived; agreed per-trip freight and platform fees are unchanged.",
    "A supplied e-way expiry that has passed blocks new departure until a current replacement is recorded. Missing expiry is explicitly not provided, with no automatic validity assumption.",
    "Departure freezes the exact supporting references then available. Later versions and destination slips do not rewrite that departure.",
    "POD freezes its own exact supporting set. The displayed pack fingerprint detects another party changing documents while a POD form is open.",
    "Documents and Trip Details show the POD references, and Supporting Trip Files links to the exact booking. Historical departures/PODs retain no fabricated references.",
    "The other party receives an in-app bell for additions/replacements. Existing scoped dispute-review POD permissions govern staff downloads and transactional Review audit events."
  ],
